+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the same JSON Schema it exposes to providers before an executor receives model input.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Missing required input returns a readable ToolResponse naming the required property without invoking the executor; accepted input, including unknown keys, is delivered exactly once without coercion or defaults, and unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects missing required input and passes accepted input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L19)).
+- Wrong types and enum violations return property paths and failed constraints without executing the tool or exposing input values in returned text or logs ([validated by: rejects type and enum violations without disclosing input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L41)).
+- Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten subsequent executions reuse the compiled schema without reading it again ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- Function-valued definitions validate against the schema resolved for the current call and cache compilation by resolved schema object identity ([validated by: uses the current dynamic schema and caches each resolved schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+
+## Integration and delivery
+
+A validation rejection is a tool result for the model's next round; the existing five-round limit bounds retries. The execute method's one-line comment points here for the rejection contract and unknown-name exception. Executor failures retain their existing behavior.
+
+README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md must describe the enforced schema, unmodified extra properties and model-visible rejection. The validator belongs in runtime dependencies. Release delivery requires a MINOR version, an npm-facing changelog entry and the executor migration note from #37.
